      {
        "question_text": "Calculate $6.38+2.754$.",
        "solution_text": "Write $6.38$ as $6.380$ and line up the decimal points.\n$0+4=4$ thousandths.\n$8+5=13$ hundredths: write $3$ hundredths and carry $1$ tenth.\n$3+7+1=11$ tenths: write $1$ tenth and carry $1$ one.\n$6+2+1=9$ ones.\n$6.38+2.754=9.134$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Calculate $12.4-2.758$.",
        "solution_text": "Write $12.4$ as $12.400$ and line up the decimal points.\nRegroup $12.400$ as $11$ ones, $13$ tenths, $9$ hundredths and $10$ thousandths.\n$10-8=2$ thousandths.\n$9-5=4$ hundredths.\n$13-7=6$ tenths.\n$11-2=9$ ones.\n$12.4-2.758=9.642$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Calculate $4.27-1.8$ by counting up.",
        "solution_text": "Count up from $1.8$ to $4.27$.\n$1.8+0.2=2$\n$2+2.27=4.27$\nAdd the two increases.\n$0.2+2.27=2.47$\n$4.27-1.8=2.47$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Find the missing numbers.\n(a) $\\square+2.846=8.3$\n(b) $11.07-\\square=6.825$",
        "solution_text": "(a) Subtract the known part from the total.\n$8.300-2.846=5.454$\n$\\square=5.454$\nCheck: $5.454+2.846=8.300$.\n(b) Subtract the remaining number from the starting number.\n$11.070-6.825=4.245$\n$\\square=4.245$\nCheck: $11.070-4.245=6.825$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A student writes $7.3-0.846=6.554$.\nCheck the calculation using place value and give the correct result.",
        "solution_text": "Write $7.3$ as $7.300$ to align the place values.\nRegroup $7.300$ as $6$ ones, $12$ tenths, $9$ hundredths and $10$ thousandths.\n$10-6=4$ thousandths.\n$9-4=5$ hundredths.\n$12-8=4$ tenths.\n$6-0=6$ ones.\n$7.300-0.846=6.454$\nThe student's result is incorrect.\nCheck by addition: $6.454+0.846=7.300$."
      }
